{"type":"text","timestamp":1787413562365,"sessionID":"ses_fd5dba979ffev5KuJNoCA7mU49","part":{"id":"prt_02a267b7d001Itm081M2Tp1d9h","messageID":"msg_02a266fa5001WQMvjZmTH06VBP","sessionID":"ses_fd5dba979ffev5KuJNoCA7mU49","type":"text","text":"The implementation is complete. Summary of changes to `lib/glob-match.js`:\n\n- Added `buildIgnoreMatcher` that builds the ignore matcher with callbacks/ignore stripped from its options, so ignore evaluation never inherits or fires the caller's callbacks.\n- Leaf matcher now: applies `ignore`, sets `result.isMatch` to the final decision, and fires `onResult` (always), `onMatch` (only when matched), `onIgnore` (only when it matched the pattern but was excluded by ignore — never when it never matched the pattern).\n- Array matcher routes through the same logic once per input (callbacks stripped from sub-matchers to avoid duplicate invocation), preserving the original boolean return.\n- The `returnObject` form and `isMatch` results are unchanged; the result object still carries `glob`, `regex`, `input`, `output`, and `isMatch` (plus the existing `state`/`posix`/`match`).\n\nExisting test failures (5) are pre-existing and unrelated to this change.","time":{"start":1787413560189,"end":1787413562358}}}
